//! AWS's published RSA-2048 public certificates for verifying an instance identity document, one per region.
//!
//! **Pinned as data, with where they came from.** Source: the Amazon EC2 User Guide, "Use the RSA-2048 signature to verify the
//! instance identity document" (<https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/verify-rsa2048.html>). The certificates here
//! were read on 2026-11-17 from the guide's last published Markdown source
//! (<https://github.com/awsdocs/amazon-ec2-user-guide>, `doc_source/verify-rsa2048.md`), because the live page is rendered by
//! script. All 31 have a 2048-bit RSA key and expire in 2195 or later.
//!
//! **Refreshing them is a reviewed change, never a runtime fetch:** compare a certificate with the live page, change this file,
//! and the unit test pins the count and the key size. A region that is not in this list (AWS adds regions; this list is the
//! guide's, not AWS's complete set) is refused as `unknown-region`, never accepted on a guessed key.
//!
//! Each row: region code, the guide's name for it, the certificate (base64 DER, as published).

/// Where the table came from.
pub const SOURCE_URL: &str =
    "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/verify-rsa2048.html";

